<title>HONG KONG: COSCO, Henderson weak after placements.</title>
<headline>COSCO, Henderson weak after placements.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in COSCO Pacific and Henderson Land slipped in heavy volume on Tuesday following share placements by both companies.</p>
<p>COSCO Pacific was down HK$0.25 at HK$6.30 on volume of 256 million shares. Goldman Sachs said COSCO was placing 250 million shares at HK$6.20 each to finance container purchases.</p>
<p>Henderson Land fell HK$1.75 to HK$64.50 on 58 million shares. On Monday, 55 million shares were placed at HK$64.00.</p>
<p>&quot;They are taking some liquidity out the market,&quot; said Rory McAllister at HSBC James Capel. Market turnover was HK$6.19 billion after 45 minutes of trade.</p>
